  "body": "Some homes are bought for today. The rarest are bought for the generations that follow.\r\n\r\nPositioned directly on the golden sands of Milford Beach, this absolute beachfront residence offers a rare opportunity to secure one of the most tightly held coastal addresses on Auckland's premium North Shore. Framed by uninterrupted sea views across the Hauraki Gulf to Rangitoto Island, this luxury waterfront home offers a lifestyle defined by prestige and a connection to the sea that very few New Zealand homes can match.\r\n\r\nLuxury is not defined by what can be added. It is defined by what can never be replaced. Beachfront positions of this calibre cannot be recreated.\r\n\r\nWhere the Lawn Ends, Milford Beach Begins\r\nElevated just above the sand, the residence opens through a private garden gate, five steps from the beach. Direct beach access of this kind is exceptionally rare among Auckland waterfront homes.\r\n\r\nLiving spaces embrace the ever changing coastal outlook. The kitchen, dining room, living room and sunroom flow seamlessly together, extending to the terrace, lawn and sand beyond, the indoor outdoor living that defines New Zealand's finest beachfront homes. Vaulted ceilings and skylights add warmth, scale and natural light, drawing the eye to the seascape and creating a home equally suited to relaxed living and effortless entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe grounds are low maintenance, offering the genuine lock up and leave lifestyle so rarely found in a true absolute beachfront setting. Double internal access garaging and off street parking complete the picture.\r\n\r\nLong summer lunches on the terrace. Children and grandchildren running barefoot from the lawn to the sand. Boats gliding across the Hauraki Gulf towards Milford Marina, dolphins offshore, and evenings that linger long after the sun has slipped behind the Auckland skyline. Sunrise over Rangitoto Island, walkers, swimmers and kayakers sharing the shoreline year round. Life beside the sea at Milford Beach is never quite the same two days running.\r\n\r\nWithin walking distance of Milford Village, with its boutiques, cafes and restaurants, along with beautiful coastal reserves and Milford Marina, this residence offers absolute beachfront living without compromising convenience. Quality healthcare is close, and Auckland City, with its commercial, cultural and international travel links, is a short drive across the Harbour Bridge.\r\n\r\nFamilies will appreciate a position in zone for Milford School and for Westlake Boys' High School and Westlake Girls' High School, three of the North Shore's most sought after state schools. Kristin School is a short drive north in Albany, internationally recognised for its International Baccalaureate (IB) programme.\r\n\r\nThis beachfront home qualifies under New Zealand's Active Investor Plus (AIP) programme, making it one of the country's very few AIP qualified absolute beachfront homes. For eligible international purchasers, opportunities of this kind are limited, and equally compelling for New Zealand, Australian and Singaporean buyers.\r\n\r\nEnjoy it exactly as it stands or enhance it over time. Its position on the sand can never be recreated. This is more than a home. It is one of New Zealand's truly irreplaceable beachfront addresses, a place where memories endure, where legacies begin and where your story continues.\r\n\r\nView the digital booklet here: https://tr.ee/9HolidayRoad_DigitalBooklet\r\n\r\nPresented by PARKER | MARMONT\r\n\r\nThis property may be marketed as suitable for overseas purchasers. However, this does not constitute confirmation of eligibility, approval, or suitability for any individual buyer. All overseas purchasers remain subject to New Zealand's overseas investment laws, including the Overseas Investment Act 2005, and may require consent from the Overseas Investment Office. You must obtain your own independent legal, financial, and technical advice and secure any necessary approvals before proceeding with a purchase.",
